<title>USA: U.S. January PPI energy goods prices.</title>
<headline>U.S. January PPI energy goods prices.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Labor Department reported energy components of the producer price index as follows, with comparisons (1982=100 unless stated otherwise).</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:	 Seasonally Adj.	Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				 Jan    Dec--(Prev)   Jan97/96</p>
<p> Finished Energy Goods    -0.2    3.4    3.1    10.4</p>
<p> -Gasoline		     2.6    4.0    5.2    19.7</p>
<p> -Heating Oil		 -2.8    5.0    4.9    17.9</p>
<p> -Residential Gas-Y	  5.0    0.9    1.7    15.6</p>
<p>Y-Dec 1990=100.</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:	 Seasonally Adj.	Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				 Jan    Dec--(Prev)   Jan97/96</p>
<p> Intermed.Energy Goods     1.1    2.2    2.5     9.8</p>
<p> -Liq.Petroleum Gas-Z	5.6    9.3    9.3    62.3</p>
<p> -Jet Fuel		     3.2    5.2    7.8    18.8</p>
<p> -Diesel Fuel		 -2.0    5.2    6.2    17.5</p>
<p> -Residual Fuel-Z	    6.6   -1.6   -1.6    18.5</p>
<p>Z-Current data not seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:	 Seasonally Adj.	Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				 Jan    Dec--(Prev)   Jan97/96</p>
<p> Crude Energy Materials   12.9   16.5   16.5    50.1</p>
<p> -Coal-Z			 3.0   -0.4   -0.4     5.3</p>
<p> -Natural Gas-Z	     21.6   34.1   34.1    84.0</p>
<p> -Petroleum-Z		  4.1    3.9    3.9    32.1</p>
<p>Note-Crude energy materials include crude petroleum.</p>
<p>Z-Current data not seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>The January report reflects the department's annual recalculation of seasonal adjustment factors.</p>
</text>
